lled Artemis uses his uncle's  old officer's coat to dismiss the cadet  guarding the body and remove its heart  throwing everyone off Landorus Trail  Landor later removes Ballinger's heart  and the hearts of local livestock to  give Credence to the perception that  there's a Madman on the loose  one of the chief pleasures of the pale  blue eyes the way it exists as a  Pastiche of what we know will be  recurring themes in the real Edgar Allan  Poe's work I've learned more in rooms  like this than any classroom you could  think of the film as sort of a prequel  or superhero origin story for Poe his  brief and doomed romance with Leah  inspires him to recite a poem a  fictional one by novelist Lewis Bayard  that references both Lenore and the pale  blue eye that gives the story its title  Endless Night caught her then in its  slurry shrouding all but a pale blue art  the name of Lenore was often used by  real world Poe in his work usually when  a poem's narrator mentions a doomed lost  love over the course of his life Poe  lost his birth mother adopted mother and  wife to premature deaths so Leah fits  right into a pattern of pale sickly  Muses for pose macop work it's no wonder  that it's love at first sight the phrase  pale blue eye appears in Poe's short  story The Tell-Tale Heart in reference  to the murder victim whose heart drives  the narrator mad from beneath the  floorboards so ascribing it to Leah and  the pale blue eye foreshadows her  premature death in and grizzly  association with excised hearts  the morning after Ballinger attacks Poe  in the woods for his interest in Leah  he's found hanged and mutilated this  casts suspicion on Poe who is  understandably angry but it's yet  another red herring as we learn Landor  killed the arrogance and aggressive  Cadets but what's inexplicable is the  fact that Ballinger didn't destroy Fry's  diary which implicated him in the attack  on Maddie by sending it to Fry's mother  instead of just burning it Ballinger  marked himself for a brutal death we  don't get to know Ballinger particularly  well so we don't know what motivates him  to send the diary to Fry's mother along  with a note that implies she may wish to  burn it there's no way he could have  known that she would instead innocently  hand it over to the very man that killed  her son then come after him but it's at  best unwise to leave it out there  although the pale blue eye has been  modestly successful with critics the  performances of Christian Bale and Harry  melling have been overlooked this award  season in a dense screenplay that  reveals little of either character's  inner life the bond between the retired  detective and the odd young Cadets is  given depth and warmth by the actors  Harry melling well beyond my imagination  bringing the poe that I envisioned to  life and it really hits when Poe  realizes he's been used by landlord to  frame the Marquis family for his  misdeeds it's a shocking betrayal but  it's not entirely clear why Landor  enlisted Poe's assistance to begin with  when he learns Fry's heart has gone  missing land or perhaps intuitively  realizes that the organ thieves might  provide him the exact cover he needs to  kill his daughter's other attackers he  then recruits the Bright Young poet  hoping that he was clever enough to  solve that mystery but not so clever  that he would put the entire situation  together it nearly worked but in letting  his guard down about Maddie he revealed  too much to his new protege  the pale blue eye maintains an  unsettling Aura of Mystery by never  revealing exactly what the Marquis  family does with the stolen Hearts it's  some sort of a cult ritual that involves  a magic circle and leaves a fair amount  of blood behind Dr Marquis believes his  daughter is communion with the spirits  of the Dead epilepsy has historically  been associated with seeing visions and  hearing voices and many contemporary  psychiatrists believe Joan of Arc  suffered from it but he doe